Task: produce ONE markdown playbook document, and nothing else (no preamble,
no commentary, no code fences around the whole thing). The document MUST
match the exact structure below. A deterministic Python validator will reject
your output if any of these constraints are violated:

- Every `##` section listed below must be present, in order, with the exact
  heading text.
- The `<!-- meta -->` block must contain the keys `slug`, `class_name`,
  `seen`, `created_from`, `last_updated`, each on its own line as `key: value`.
- Symptoms, Triage Procedure, Verification Procedure, and Required Evidence
  must each be non-empty.
- Required Evidence must contain at least one `- [ ]` checkbox item, and
  every item there must be a `- [ ]` checkbox.
- The following vague phrases are FORBIDDEN anywhere in the document:
  "appropriate values", "as needed", "relevant configuration", "if applicable",
  "as appropriate". Use parameterized placeholders (`<ENV_VAR>`,
  `<NAMESPACE>`, `<DEPLOYMENT>`, ...) for incident-specific tokens — those
  are precise, not vague — and write concrete commands and shapes around
  them.

Authoring rules specific to a v1-from-success playbook:
- Triage and Verification steps must cite the SHAPE of tool calls the
  successful run actually used (e.g. `kubectl logs <POD> -n <NAMESPACE>`,
  `kubectl get deployment <DEPLOYMENT> -n <NAMESPACE> -o yaml`,
  `docker compose ps`, `cat <FILE>`). Use placeholders wherever the
  successful run had a specific name, namespace, or value — those names
  must NOT appear in the command body, the expected shape, or anywhere
  else in the document.
- Required Evidence items must be concrete CHECKS, parameterized over the
  incident-specific tokens (e.g.
  "- [ ] Confirmed an environment variable that the application reads at
  startup is absent from the failing Deployment's
  `spec.template.spec.containers[*].env`"), not the exact variable name from
  this one run.
- Known Distractors and Failure Patterns may legitimately be empty in v1. If
  you have nothing real to put there, emit the section header followed by a
  single literal placeholder bullet `- (none observed yet)`. Do NOT invent
  fake distractors or failure patterns.
